Goal:
The password for the next level is in the same filename with it being the only human readable 
string preceded by ' = '.

Approach:
A brute force way would be to cat the file and grep for the '=' but the file being a data file it 
is not possible.
My approach would be to convert it strings somehow and find the command which could do (using google)
LOL.

Command 
strings data.txt | grep =

Breakdown
The command is pretty straightforward, but the first part of the pipe is used to convert the data 
content into strings and the latter part fo the pipe is used to filter content with only = in them.

